<x-layout :information-unavailable="$informationUnavailable" title="Privacy notice"><section class="container page-heading"><span class="eyebrow">Your information</span><h1>Privacy, clearly.</h1><p>Draft notice · pending venue approval before booking, messaging, and chatbot services open.</p></section><section class="container section prose"><h2>What this version does</h2><p>You can browse the public pages without creating an account. When online booking is enabled by the venue, you can submit a reservation request without an account. Published tournaments may accept registration without an account.</p><h2>Booking information</h2><p>Reservation requests collect your name, phone number, chosen table, schedule, and quoted price. Authorized staff use these details to review and manage your booking. Your private reference code allows status lookup; keep it confidential. Tournament registrations collect your name, phone number, selected event, and quoted entry fee. For paid tournaments, you submit a GCash transaction reference and a payment screenshot. Only authorized staff can open the screenshot to verify the transfer. CueLab removes the screenshot 30 days after the tournament ends and keeps the payment and review records. Registration status is available using a private reference code. Contact messaging will describe its data use before opening.</p><h2>Local browser storage</h2><p>Your theme preference is saved in your browser. The website also uses essential session and security cookies.</p><h2>AI disclosure</h2><p>CueChat uses Dify and Gemini to interpret questions and find approved venue information. If you use CueChat, your message and any booking date, time, duration, or table preference in the chat draft may be processed by those services. Enter contact details and private references only in the website booking forms.</p><h2>Access, retention, and questions</h2><p>The venue’s privacy contact, retention period, hosting arrangements, and process for access or correction requests are pending confirmation. This notice must be completed before customer information is collected.</p><a class="text-link" href="{{ route('contact') }}">View contact information ↗</a></section></x-layout>
